<%# The drawer for everything a form shouldn't open with (D16): capture asks
    for the thing itself, and the settings the assistant can decide for you
    fold away in here. A layout partial on purpose — it never learns what's
    inside it, so adding a control later means adding it to the block at the
    call site rather than teaching this file about a new primitive.

    `hint` puts the state of the drawer's contents on the closed line, so
    folding something away doesn't hide whether it needs attention; `open`
    is for when it does (a validation error in here is invisible otherwise). %>
<details class="rounded-xl border border-edge px-3 py-2" <%= "open" if local_assigns[:open] %>>
  <summary class="cursor-pointer text-sm font-medium text-ink">
    Advanced<% if local_assigns[:hint].present? %><span class="font-normal text-soft"> — <%= hint %></span><% end %>
  </summary>

  <div class="mt-3 space-y-4"><%= yield %></div>
</details>
